sections.text:
The commonest mistakes are measuring from an unclear drawing without asking, and forgetting items that are easy to miss, such as excavation, disposal, damp-proof courses, lintels and sundries.

Others are:
writing descriptions too vague to price;
mixing units, or adding quantities in different units;
leaving out builder’s work in connection with services;
ignoring the conditions of contract when valuing changes;
treating software output as correct because it looks neat.

Also state your assumptions. A marker, like a client, needs to see how you reached the figure.
